  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 18 is the longest at Northside at 707 feet — a closing par 4 that brings everything together: the USDGC-style length, the woods, and the water hazards that define the course. Three committed shots to a finish that feels earned. It's the hole that makes you glad you came back for the back nine.",
  "localTips": "Avoid Sunday services (9am–1pm). The long par 4s on holes 1, 14, and 18 are the heart of the course; the four water hazards are the heartbreak. Free to play and very cart friendly.",
